    "cover": "slide-037.webp",
    "category": "Buyer Resources",
    "intro": "A wholesale sports bottle buying guide covering practical lid styles, carrying design, materials and branded collections. These checkpoints focus on real sampling, documentation and commercial decisions for the exact plastic drinkware model.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Map the product to how athletes actually use it",
        "paragraph": "Gym users, commuters, cyclists and outdoor customers may prefer different opening mechanisms and capacities. Identify how the bottle will be carried and filled, whether one-handed drinking matters and how often the lid will be opened. A great-looking water bottle may underperform if its cap is awkward, cleaning is difficult or the handle feels insecure under a full load."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Compare caps and carrying accessories",
        "paragraph": "Options can include screw lids, flip lids, spouts, straws, loops or larger handles. Each closure creates different sealing and cleaning points. Confirm which lid is included with the exact SKU and whether alternatives fit the same bottle neck. Do not promise cross-compatibility solely because two caps appear to thread onto the same bottle."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Choose capacities for the channel",
        "paragraph": "A compact bottle may fit bags and cup holders, while a larger jug reduces refill frequency but becomes heavier and bulkier. Ask for actual measurements and empty weight, not only the marketing volume. Decide whether a printed or molded graduation scale is important. If multiple capacities will share a brand design, verify print placement and available colors separately for each model."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Select realistic material requirements",
        "paragraph": "Discuss PC, Tritan, PP and PETG according to the desired appearance, usage conditions and destination requirements. Confirm the exact polymer grade of the body and each food-contact cap component. A BPA-free or dishwasher-safe description requires product-specific support. Material changes may alter print adhesion, transparency and tooling fit."
